{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>You shall make tassels for yourself.</b> The tzitzit are called גדלים. And our Rabbis of blessed memory received that the reason the passage of tzitzit was juxtaposed to kilayim (mixed species) is to teach that the commandment of tzitzit overrides the prohibition of kilayim, and we expound juxtapositions: for if it did not come to permit kilayim through the commandment of tzitzit, why did He need to mention the prohibition of kilayim here and juxtapose it to the commandment of tzitzit — and behold, it is already mentioned in the section Kedoshim. And the secret of the commandment of tzitzit I have already mentioned in its place in the parashah of ויאמר (Numbers 15). And the term גדילים that He mentions here for the garment of tzitzit is an allusion to what is written (Psalms 104): ״ה׳ אלהי גדלת מאד הוד והדר לבשת״, and understand this, for one who dons tzitzit with ל״ב threads is a model of this, and this is clear." "<b>On the four corners of your garment.</b> From what is written in the passage of tzitzit (there): ״על כנפי בגדיהם״ — one might understand a person to be obligated in tzitzit for anything called a בגד, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 28): ״ואלה הבגדים אשר יעשו חשן ואפוד ומעיל״ — and even if it has only two corners or three, since it says ״כנפי בגדיהם״. But this verse now reveals that the obligation of tzitzit does not apply to every garment unless it has four corners, like tallitot and sheets and similar items. And a garment with two or three corners is exempt from tzitzit, since it says ״ארבע.״ But one with five is obligated in tzitzit, for in the inclusive category of five there are four. And thus our Rabbis of blessed memory said: ״על ארבע כנפות כסותך״ — four and not three. You say four and not three, or is it only four and not five? When it says ״אשר תכסה בה״ — behold, one of five is stated. What then do I fulfill by ״ארבע״? Four and not three. And what did you see to include one of five and exclude one of three? I include one of five, for in the category of five there are four, and I exclude one of three, for in the category of three there are not four."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Hebrew citations normalized: תהלים ק\"ד = Psalms 104; במדבר ט\"ו = Numbers 15. ל״ב (32) threads copied as written.", 1 "Hebrew citations normalized: שמות כ\"ח = Exodus 28. The Talmudic passage is from Menachot 43b."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:28.188408398Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}